{
  "id": "m10-fewest-stops",
  "title": "Fewest Refuels",
  "source": {
    "name": "Classic greedy (jump game / gas stations)"
  },
  "rating": 1300,
  "tags": [
    "greedy",
    "sorting"
  ],
  "statement": "A car starts at position `0` with a full tank and must reach position `D` on a line. A full tank lets it drive exactly `K` units. There are `n` fuel stations at positions `p_i` (`0 < p_i < D`, several may share a position); at a station the car may refuel to full. Print the minimum number of refuels needed to reach `D`, or `-1` if it is impossible.\n\n**Input.** First line `D K n`. Second line: the `n` station positions (not necessarily sorted).\n\n**Output.** One integer.",
  "constraints": [
    "1 ≤ n ≤ 2000 in this browser version (the idea scales to 2·10^5)",
    "1 ≤ D, K ≤ 10^9"
  ],
  "timeLimitMs": 2000,
  "hints": [
    "Sort the stations. Think about which stations you could have reached on the current tank.",
    "Among all stations you can reach, which one gives the largest future reach?",
    "Greedy: keep `reach`. While `reach < D`, scan every station at or before `reach`, take the farthest `p + K`; if nothing improves `reach`, print -1."
  ],
  "editorial": "Maintain `reach`, the farthest point reachable with the refuels used so far. All stations with `p <= reach` are candidates for the next refuel and refuelling at the farthest one yields the largest new reach `p + K`; refuelling at any other candidate is dominated (exchange argument: it reaches a subset of what the farthest one reaches, so swapping never hurts). Each refuel scans new stations only, so after sorting the work is linear: `O(n log n)`. If no scanned station extends `reach`, the destination is unreachable.",
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(n log n)",
    "space": "O(n)"
  },
  "starter": {
    "python": "import sys\nd = sys.stdin.read().split()\nD, K, n = int(d[0]), int(d[1]), int(d[2])\np = sorted(map(int, d[3:3 + n]))\n# greedy over stations\n",
    "javascript": "const [D, K, n] = readLine().split(' ').map(Number);\nconst p = readLine().split(' ').map(Number).sort((a, b) => a - b);\n// greedy over stations\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        // D K n, then n positions\n    }\n}\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    long long D, K; int n; cin >> D >> K >> n;  // greedy: refuel at the farthest reachable station\n    return 0;\n}\n"
  },
  "solutions": {
    "python": "import sys\nd = sys.stdin.read().split()\nD, K, n = int(d[0]), int(d[1]), int(d[2])\np = sorted(map(int, d[3:3 + n]))\nreach = K\nstops = 0\ni = 0\nwhile reach < D:\n    far = reach\n    while i < n and p[i] <= reach:\n        far = max(far, p[i] + K)\n        i += 1\n    if far == reach:\n        print(-1)\n        break\n    stops += 1\n    reach = far\nelse:\n    print(stops)\n",
    "javascript": "const lines = [];\nlet line;\nwhile ((line = readLine()) !== null) lines.push(line);\nconst tok = lines.join(' ').split(/\\s+/).filter(s => s.length);\nconst D = Number(tok[0]), K = Number(tok[1]), n = Number(tok[2]);\nconst p = tok.slice(3, 3 + n).map(Number).sort((a, b) => a - b);\nlet reach = K, stops = 0, i = 0, ans = null;\nwhile (reach < D) {\n  let far = reach;\n  while (i < n && p[i] <= reach) {\n    far = Math.max(far, p[i] + K);\n    i++;\n  }\n  if (far === reach) { ans = -1; break; }\n  stops++;\n  reach = far;\n}\nconsole.log(ans === null ? stops : ans);\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long D = sc.nextLong(), K = sc.nextLong();\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        long[] p = new long[n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) p[i] = sc.nextLong();\n        Arrays.sort(p);\n        long reach = K;\n        int stops = 0, i = 0;\n        while (reach < D) {\n            long far = reach;\n            while (i < n && p[i] <= reach) {\n                far = Math.max(far, p[i] + K);\n                i++;\n            }\n            if (far == reach) {\n                System.out.println(-1);\n                return;\n            }\n            stops++;\n            reach = far;\n        }\n        System.out.println(stops);\n    }\n}\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    long long D, K;\n    int n;\n    cin >> D >> K >> n;\n    vector<long long> p(n);\n    for (auto &v : p) cin >> v;\n    sort(p.begin(), p.end());\n    long long reach = K;\n    int stops = 0, i = 0;\n    while (reach < D) {\n        long long far = reach;\n        while (i < n && p[i] <= reach) {\n            far = max(far, p[i] + K);\n            i++;\n        }\n        if (far == reach) {\n            cout << -1 << endl;\n            return 0;\n        }\n        stops++;\n        reach = far;\n    }\n    cout << stops << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n"
  },
